{"_v":1,"id":"tarzan-2006","bd":{"positive":0,"mixed":0,"negative":4},"rv":[{"cn":"Peter Marks","o":"The Washington Post","s":54,"b":"Negative","t":1,"u":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/archive/lifestyle/2006/05/11/tarzan-swings-and-mostly-misses/8a4c5e9a-9f8d-4d4a-8a1d-7f2e9c8b5d6a/","d":"2006-05-11","q":"What Disney has created is a show that looks terrific but sounds mediocre, a musical that soars literally but crashes figuratively."},{"cn":"Charles Isherwood","o":"Variety","s":46,"b":"Negative","t":1,"u":"https://variety.com/2006/film/reviews/brothers-sisters-1200513334/","d":"2006-05-10","q":"Disney's 'Tarzan' is a sporadically diverting but ultimately disappointing musical that never finds its footing in the transition from screen to stage."},{"cn":"Ben Brantley","o":"The New York Times","s":42,"b":"Negative","t":1,"u":"https://www.nytimes.com/2006/05/11/theater/reviews/11tarz.html","d":"2006-05-11","q":"Though much money (a reported $12 million to $15 million) and international research (with special emphasis on what a character in the show calls pendulation) has been lavished on \"Tarzan,\" it somehow never acquired the art of focus."},{"cn":"Eric March","o":"Theater Life","s":54,"b":"Negative","t":3,"u":"https://theaterlife.com/tarzan/","d":"2007-02-05","q":"You smile at the silliness, but most everything is jaw droopingly corny and obvious."}],"au":{"score":66,"designation":"Disliking","sources":{"mz":{"s":66,"c":77,"sr":3.3}}},"ta":"226 W 46th St, New York, NY 10036","pd":"2006-03-24","ca":[{"n":"Josh Strickland","r":"Tarzan"},{"n":"Merle Dandridge","r":"Kala"},{"n":"Jenn Gambatese","r":"Jane Porter"},{"n":"Chester Gregory II","r":"Terk"},{"n":"Shuler Hensley","r":"Kerchak"},{"n":"Timothy Jerome","r":"Professor Porter"},{"n":"Donnie R. Keshawarz","r":"Mr. Clayton"},{"n":"Daniel Manche","r":"Young Tarzan"},{"n":"Alex Rutherford","r":"Young Tarzan"},{"n":"Marcus Bellamy","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Celina Carvajal","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Dwayne Clark","r":"Ensembl